WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:03.440
Alarms go off all around the facility.

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:05.960
Things descended into chaos so quickly.

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:10.150
Of course, the staff of the SCP Foundation
are extremely familiar with the horrors of

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:14.820
a containment breach by now, but this was
something exceptional.

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:20.310
Two anomalies had joined forces in an unexpected
fashion, neutralizing some of the weaknesses

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:23.130
that the two of them usually experienced.

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:26.110
Needless to say, this was bad.

00:00:26.110 --> 00:00:30.509
More specifically, 74 dead staff members were
dead already.

00:00:30.509 --> 00:00:34.700
Several different Mobile Task Forces had already
been dispatched to hunt down this terrifying

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:40.380
new anomaly, but none of them knew where it
was hiding in the depths of the site.

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:45.920
Little did they know, this deadly new hybrid
had already escaped the SCP Foundation, and

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:49.600
was on its way towards a nearby population
center.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:52.390
That’s where the real fun would start.

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:57.110
But before we get to all that carnage, let’s
rewind the clock a little and find out how

00:00:57.110 --> 00:00:59.280
this disaster started...

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:04.059
Some things just go great together: Like peanut
butter and jelly, milk and cereal, or clicking

00:01:04.059 --> 00:01:07.799
“Subscribe” while you’re watching a
video by SCP Explained.

00:01:07.799 --> 00:01:12.240
But for every match made in Heaven, there’s
also a match made in Hell.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:17.049
Like being covered in sugar water while you
walk past a wasp nest, or doing tricks with

00:01:17.049 --> 00:01:22.619
your awesome zippo lighter next to the gas
pump, or most horrifying of them all, a combination

00:01:22.619 --> 00:01:27.219
of SCP-106 and SCP-035.

00:01:27.219 --> 00:01:32.139
Of course, the reputations of these two horrible
creatures are well known and well feared enough

00:01:32.139 --> 00:01:33.289
on their own.

00:01:33.289 --> 00:01:39.359
SCP-106 is a humanoid abomination also known
as the Old Man, capable of walking through

00:01:39.359 --> 00:01:44.580
walls and entering his own private pocket
dimension, where he practices his predilection

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:46.999
for pain to its full potential.

00:01:46.999 --> 00:01:52.649
And then there’s SCP-035, also known as
the Possessive Mask.

00:01:52.649 --> 00:01:57.299
This is one of the most powerful and dangerous
psychic entities that the SCP Foundation has

00:01:57.299 --> 00:01:59.299
in its vast collection.

00:01:59.299 --> 00:02:04.029
Some of its more minor unpleasant qualities
are things like the fact it constantly drips

00:02:04.029 --> 00:02:09.099
corrosive black slime, or the fact it immediately
reduces you to a state of brain death when

00:02:09.099 --> 00:02:11.250
you’re foolish enough to wear it.

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:15.780
On the more severe end of its abilities is
its power to crawl into the mind of anyone

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:20.540
around it, slowly whispering horrors into
their mind until they’re completely under

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:24.019
its control, or utterly broken.

00:02:24.019 --> 00:02:29.020
It likely has designs on world domination,
or at the very least, to plunge the human

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:32.900
race into an unimaginable pit of eternal suffering.

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:38.080
The one saving grace is the fact that 035’s
corrosive slime slowly destroys the body of

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:42.730
its hosts, limiting the purview of each one
of its reigns of terror.

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:47.280
But occasionally, there are wonderful, terrible
exceptions to the rule...

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:53.879
Speaking of terrible, our story began, chronologically,
with SCP-106 showing one of its rare signs

00:02:53.879 --> 00:02:54.879
of activity.

00:02:54.879 --> 00:02:59.519
This, naturally, caused waves of panic to
rock through the researchers and security

00:02:59.519 --> 00:03:00.930
staff of the site.

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:05.329
They’d need to grab a D-Class then plug
in and warm up the femur breaker.

00:03:05.329 --> 00:03:10.290
They’d also need to mobilize groups of on-site
guards with powerful flashlights to slow the

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:12.459
gnarled old monster down.

00:03:12.459 --> 00:03:17.370
But by now, SCP-106 had gotten wise to the
Foundation’s techniques.

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:20.930
He wouldn’t make himself so easy to capture
this time.

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:26.300
He wanted to have the proper time to enjoy
himself.

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:28.750
SCP-106 got up and phased through the nearby
wall.

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:34.140
His cell was never easy to escape - They filled
it with strange shapes and running water,

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:36.299
just to confuse his wretched old mind.

00:03:36.299 --> 00:03:39.340
But once he was out, he was out.

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:44.450
He avoided the hallways, instead just phasing
from wall to wall until he reached a different

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:46.280
block of containment chambers.

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:48.819
That’s where the fateful meeting would take
place.

00:03:48.819 --> 00:03:53.170
It wouldn’t be the first time he’d wandered
into other containment cells - his battle

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:59.590
with SCP-682 perhaps being the most famous
- but this time, something was different.

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:04.129
The room he’d just phased into didn’t
contain some huge, writhing monster, or another

00:04:04.129 --> 00:04:05.540
humanoid beast.

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:11.170
It contained instead a glass container on
top of a podium, the walls coated in deadly

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:14.950
Telekill alloy to keep its prisoner’s immense
psychic power sealed in.

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:21.370
But now that SCP-106 was in the room, standing
mere feet away from the grinning, white mask

00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:27.580
inside the glass container, there was nothing
keeping the two from having an extremely fateful

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:28.720
conversation.

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:34.720
The first thing SCP-106 noticed was the black
liquid leaking from the mask.

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:35.720
Strange.

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:39.360
It seemed to perfectly match his own secretions...

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:41.070
“Hello there, good sir!

00:04:41.070 --> 00:04:46.470
It isn’t often I have visitors in here,
and even less so visitors who are as handsome

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:52.530
as you,” The Mask said, speaking directly
into the old man’s frail, fractured mind.

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:55.940
“I don’t believe we’ve ever been acquainted.

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:58.530
Come a little closer and remove the glass
box.

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:00.800
I’ll be able to hear you better that way.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:04.240
Come on, come on, don’t be shy!”

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:07.850
The Old Man felt something about the Mask
was distasteful.

00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:14.000
Even to a creature as despicable as SCP-106,
something about the Mask just seemed slimy,

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.190
metaphorically as well as literally.

00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:20.870
And yet, it found itself stepping forward
towards the glass case, almost as though he

00:05:20.870 --> 00:05:22.400
was sleep walking.

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:25.340
How was the Mask invading his mind like this?

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:29.849
He’d always been one of the more mysterious
creatures in the Foundation’s containment,

00:05:29.849 --> 00:05:34.880
and yet, SCP-035 had slipped into his mind
like a warm bath.

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:37.270
On some level, it frightened him.

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:39.490
“Yes, yes, that’s wonderful!

00:05:39.490 --> 00:05:46.050
Come closer, dear boy, you’re doing so well,”
The Mask said as the Old Man reached forward

00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:47.930
and began lifting off the glass case.

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:51.979
“I think I’d look rather good on you,
don’t you agree?

00:05:51.979 --> 00:05:55.740
Let’s cover up that nasty old face of yours.

00:05:55.740 --> 00:05:59.760
You’ll look positively spiffing, old chap.

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:05.379
Just do exactly as I say, and this is all
going to go wonderfully.”

00:06:05.379 --> 00:06:11.360
The Old Man picked up the Mask, somehow not
even in control of his own body anymore.

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:16.190
An almost electrical power seemed to pulse
out of the Mask and through the Old Man’s

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:17.770
rotting fingertips.

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:23.440
The Old Man was a sadist, but he’d never
before encountered this kind of utterly malicious

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:25.020
intelligence.

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:29.940
This was a mind geared to commit almost incalculable
evil, and while the Old Man was wondering

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:35.740
how exactly he felt about that, he was already
lifting the Mask up to his face, and watching

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:38.610
the universe go very, very dark.

00:06:38.610 --> 00:06:43.580
Outside, a small army of Foundation security
operatives, armed with flashlights and assault

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:48.500
rifles, were charging through the halls, trying
to trace the movements of the Old Man for

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:49.500
recapture.

00:06:49.500 --> 00:06:54.680
Back in the Old Man’s cell, a confused serial
arsonist was being shoved into the femur breaker

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:58.380
by a group of nervous and impatient researchers.

00:06:58.380 --> 00:07:02.580
None of them knew they were dealing with an
entirely different beast down here now.

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:07.700
Eventually, the security team found the last
rusty scorch mark on the wall of a containment

00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:08.700
cell...

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:12.070
Belonging to SCP-035.

00:07:12.070 --> 00:07:16.430
Before they could even comprehend the terrifying
implications of this horrible scenario, they

00:07:16.430 --> 00:07:19.530
charged into the cell in hopes of stopping
it.

00:07:19.530 --> 00:07:25.419
But by the time they were in there, both the
Old Man and the Mask were already gone.

00:07:25.419 --> 00:07:26.419
Well...

00:07:26.419 --> 00:07:27.419
Not entirely.

00:07:27.419 --> 00:07:31.500
Suddenly, the guards in the room felt an odd
sense of calm wash over them.

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:38.030
Not a true, authentic calm, but an artificially
induced one, like the lulling of cattle while

00:07:38.030 --> 00:07:40.560
a bolt gun descends towards their foreheads.

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:45.550
The Mask’s psychic influence had pacified
them, making them perfect prey for the rotten

00:07:45.550 --> 00:07:49.680
hands reaching out from the ground, and pulling
them down into oblivion.

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:53.229
The guards outside heard the most horrific
screaming.

00:07:53.229 --> 00:07:57.389
They circled the door, terrified, aiming everything
they had at the entryway.

00:07:57.389 --> 00:07:58.880
But it wouldn’t be enough.

00:07:58.880 --> 00:08:08.289
Soon enough, this new hybrid beast - SCP-106
wearing SCP-035 - emerged, and began its onslaught.

00:08:08.289 --> 00:08:14.270
It had the immense physical abilities of 106,
bolstered by 035’s diabolical intelligence

00:08:14.270 --> 00:08:20.340
and ability to cloud the minds of its victims,
inhibiting their capacity to run away or fight

00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:21.340
back.

00:08:21.340 --> 00:08:26.370
But most frightening of all: Because SCP-106
was already adapted to resist the effect of

00:08:26.370 --> 00:08:32.200
its own corrosive mucus, it was also perfectly
able to sustain the Mask as a host without

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:34.800
ever melting and falling apart.

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:36.729
See what we mean about a match made in hell?

00:08:36.729 --> 00:08:39.560
“How do you like my new body, gentlemen?”

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:42.890
The Mask asked, its voice dripping with malicious
glee.

00:08:42.890 --> 00:08:47.700
“It isn’t much to look at, I know, but
you’re about to get very well acquainted

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:51.520
with its collection of charming abilities...”

00:08:51.520 --> 00:08:53.579
And the Mask stayed true to its word.

00:08:53.579 --> 00:08:58.779
It rampaged through the containment site,
waltzing through walls like a gleeful schoolchild

00:08:58.779 --> 00:09:04.560
with the heart and mind of the devil himself,
leaving a pile of melted, tortured corpses

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:05.560
in its wake.

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:08.899
Researchers, guards, janitorial staff.

00:09:08.899 --> 00:09:10.510
Nobody was safe.

00:09:10.510 --> 00:09:15.670
And with every killing, the rest of the staff
became increasingly afraid, only strengthening

00:09:15.670 --> 00:09:17.910
the psychic hold of the Mask.

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:22.680
It was having the best day it could remember
in a long time.

00:09:22.680 --> 00:09:27.010
The Site Director and his team put out a mayday
for all available Mobile Task Force units

00:09:27.010 --> 00:09:31.090
to descend onto the area and help them deal
with this deadly new threat.

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:36.930
But by the time they were on their way, the
Mask and its new SCP-106 body had already

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:39.459
had its fun with the Foundation.

00:09:39.459 --> 00:09:43.080
Even when they activated the femur breaker,
nothing happened.

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:48.519
The Mask was far more interested in the pain
it could cause outside, and far too intelligent

00:09:48.519 --> 00:09:52.600
to be lured back into imprisonment by such
a simple trick.

00:09:52.600 --> 00:09:57.290
Instead, the hybrid made its way out of the
nearby perimeter wall, finding its way to

00:09:57.290 --> 00:10:02.550
a heavily armored Foundation ground vehicle
and sliding in through the door like a ghost.

00:10:02.550 --> 00:10:06.459
The operative in the driver’s seat was immediately
terrified by the monster suddenly sitting

00:10:06.459 --> 00:10:11.110
next to it, but then, the Mask’s psychic
effects took over his mind.

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:16.589
He became a calm, placid little servant, just
like all those other mortal fools.

00:10:16.589 --> 00:10:21.420
“I feel like a change of scenery, old sport,”
the Mask said to him.

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:26.000
“Take me out to the nearest city, it can
be one of your choosing.

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:28.930
I feel like having a little night on the town.

00:10:28.930 --> 00:10:32.100
It’s been far too long, you know...”

00:10:32.100 --> 00:10:34.959
The hypnotized driver nodded and punched the
gas.

00:10:34.959 --> 00:10:39.139
The guards were too busy controlling the aftermath
of the chaos within the site to even notice

00:10:39.139 --> 00:10:42.310
the creature they were chasing had already
escaped.

00:10:42.310 --> 00:10:47.310
And if it reached a nearby city, then the
chaos, cruelty, and madness it was liable

00:10:47.310 --> 00:10:52.860
to release would be the biggest mess the Foundation
would need to clean up in quite some time.

00:10:52.860 --> 00:10:56.920
Which was precisely what the malicious Mask
had in mind.

00:10:56.920 --> 00:11:00.490
Meanwhile, Dr. Robert Scranton woke up in
a dark room.

00:11:00.490 --> 00:11:04.860
Well, he wasn’t sure if it was a room, but
it was definitely dark.

00:11:04.860 --> 00:11:10.279
He rose to his feet in this strange, black
void, surrounded on all sides by blackness.

00:11:10.279 --> 00:11:14.480
It wasn’t the belly of SCP-3001 - the dreaded
Red Reality - again.

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:20.709
No, this was something new, and what’s more,
he had no idea how on Earth he’d gotten

00:11:20.709 --> 00:11:21.800
here...

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:26.310
“Dr. Scranton!” said a cruel, mocking
voice behind him.

00:11:26.310 --> 00:11:27.910
“Turn around, old chap.

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:33.070
It’s been far too long since I’ve seen
you in the flesh.

00:11:33.070 --> 00:11:36.360
Well, in a manner of speaking, at least...”

00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:42.800
Confused, Dr. Scranton turned and saw a vaguely
familiar sight - SCP-035, the Possessive Mask

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:45.000
- floating in the dark behind him.

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:47.420
What on Earth was happening here, he wondered?

00:11:47.420 --> 00:11:52.620
“Oh, you really don’t remember, do you?”

00:11:52.620 --> 00:11:57.199
The Mask said with a spiteful laugh, replying
to a thought he’d never voiced aloud.

00:11:57.199 --> 00:11:59.660
“We’re in your mind, Doctor!

00:11:59.660 --> 00:12:03.980
As it turns out, you’re harder to erase
than I thought, perhaps because you’re buried

00:12:03.980 --> 00:12:06.620
so deep in the psyche of that monster.

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:11.399
No matter, I’ll get you eventually..”

00:12:11.399 --> 00:12:14.019
How strange, Dr. Scranton thought.

00:12:14.019 --> 00:12:16.829
This must be his mind playing tricks on him
somehow.

00:12:16.829 --> 00:12:21.209
He raised a hand to scratch his head quizzically,
and only then realized that his right hand

00:12:21.209 --> 00:12:24.699
was gone, simply vanished from the end of
his wrist.

00:12:24.699 --> 00:12:26.380
The Mask gave another sick laugh.

00:12:26.380 --> 00:12:27.380
“Ooh, it’s already started!

00:12:27.380 --> 00:12:36.370
I told you I’d get you, Scranton,” The
Mask said.

00:12:36.370 --> 00:12:41.710
“I never normally get to delete a mind slowly.

00:12:41.710 --> 00:12:43.490
This will be amusing.”

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:45.389
“Where’s Anna?”

00:12:45.389 --> 00:12:48.480
Scranton asked, suddenly wondering about the
safety of his beloved wife.

00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:53.790
He couldn’t help but worry when this got
another cruel laugh out of the Mask.

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:58.110
“Don’t you remember, Robert?”

00:12:58.110 --> 00:12:59.970
The Mask said, through giggles.

00:12:59.970 --> 00:13:02.790
“You killed her.

00:13:02.790 --> 00:13:06.260
You killed her with your toxic embrace.

00:13:06.260 --> 00:13:08.959
She died terrified of you.”

00:13:08.959 --> 00:13:12.610
And with that, all the awful memories came
flooding back...

00:13:12.610 --> 00:13:15.730
Back in the real world, things weren’t any
less horrifying.

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:20.510
When the vehicle had finally made its way
to the nearest city, the Masked Old Man had

00:13:20.510 --> 00:13:25.990
unceremoniously murdered its chauffeur and
decided to go for a little explore.

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:30.930
It’d been so long since it felt the sun
on its pristine white porcelain.

00:13:30.930 --> 00:13:33.050
Such a beautiful day outside.

00:13:33.050 --> 00:13:35.720
It couldn’t wait to kill some people around
here.

00:13:35.720 --> 00:13:41.370
It began its rampage in a dark alley, snatching
some homeless people and unfortunate passers

00:13:41.370 --> 00:13:44.449
by through the graffiti-stained stone walls.

00:13:44.449 --> 00:13:48.640
By the time it was done with them, there weren’t
even any bones left.

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:54.040
But this would only be the start of the Masked
Old Man’s horrific rampage through the city.

00:13:54.040 --> 00:13:58.839
Next, he invaded an office building and decided
to unleash his grisly wrath on the people

00:13:58.839 --> 00:13:59.839
within.

00:13:59.839 --> 00:14:03.019
Some were pulled through the ground while
chatting at the water cooler.

00:14:03.019 --> 00:14:06.889
Others dragged through the walls as they went
to refresh their coffee.

00:14:06.889 --> 00:14:11.839
Some were simply sitting at their desks, getting
on with their daily work, when a dark silhouette

00:14:11.839 --> 00:14:13.720
appeared behind them.

00:14:13.720 --> 00:14:17.730
Some turned around, saw the creature, and
screamed immediately.

00:14:17.730 --> 00:14:23.240
Others remained in ignorance, and only screamed
when an acidic, rotting hand curled around

00:14:23.240 --> 00:14:24.570
their shoulder.

00:14:24.570 --> 00:14:27.770
But every single one of them screamed eventually.

00:14:27.770 --> 00:14:32.720
By this point, the SCP Foundation had started
sending all the Mobile Task Forces in the

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:38.990
area to the nearby city after receiving reports
of unexplainable disappearances and murders.

00:14:38.990 --> 00:14:43.710
Panic was starting to spread, and that panic
was only making the nightmarish psychic abilities

00:14:43.710 --> 00:14:45.560
of the Mask even stronger.

00:14:45.560 --> 00:14:50.520
The challenge would be intercepting SCP-106
and removing the Mask before it became too

00:14:50.520 --> 00:14:53.450
powerful for them to do anything about it.

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:58.110
If they didn’t, they could be looking at
loss of life on a massive scale.

00:14:58.110 --> 00:15:02.320
Which was exactly what SCP-035 hoped to indulge
in.

00:15:02.320 --> 00:15:06.740
A young barista was having a stressful day
at a nearby boutique coffee shop.

00:15:06.740 --> 00:15:11.800
She retired to the staff bathroom to splash
some water in her face and recenter herself.

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:16.550
She sighed and looked up from the sink into
the mirror to see if her makeup was running,

00:15:16.550 --> 00:15:17.660
then screamed.

00:15:17.660 --> 00:15:23.520
A dark figure was standing right behind her:
It looked like a rotting human corpse, dripping

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:28.990
with black slime, and wearing a grinning white
Ancient Greek comedy mask.

00:15:28.990 --> 00:15:32.230
“I’m not interrupting anything, am I?”

00:15:32.230 --> 00:15:34.510
The Masked Old Man said, amused.

00:15:34.510 --> 00:15:38.540
Soon after, the dark presence had spilled
out into the coffee shop.

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:42.690
The psychic powers of the Mask caused its
victims to be paralyzed with sheer terror,

00:15:42.690 --> 00:15:44.949
unable to escape its cruel hands.

00:15:44.949 --> 00:15:49.250
The death toll of the day had already risen
to over a hundred, and the Masked Old Man

00:15:49.250 --> 00:15:50.970
had no intention of stopping.

00:15:50.970 --> 00:15:55.480
That’s when several police cruisers skidded
to a halt in front of the coffee shop.

00:15:55.480 --> 00:15:57.759
Cops disembarked from their cars and pulled
their handguns.

00:15:57.759 --> 00:16:02.770
“Step out of the store with your hands up!”
one of them yelled over a megaphone.

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:05.610
“Any sudden moves and we’ll blow you to
kingdom come!”

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:09.579
This made the Masked Old Man laugh.

00:16:09.579 --> 00:16:14.509
Oh, how very adorable...

00:16:14.509 --> 00:16:19.470
Not long after, he was driving a police cruiser
further into town, with a pile of dead cops

00:16:19.470 --> 00:16:21.680
left in the street behind him.

00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:24.920
This was shaping up to be such a wonderful
day.

00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:27.180
He never wanted it to end.

00:16:27.180 --> 00:16:31.279
Back in the pitch dark of the mindscape, Dr.
Robert Scranton was looking a little worse

00:16:31.279 --> 00:16:32.579
for the wear.

00:16:32.579 --> 00:16:37.190
Both of his legs had disappeared, along with
one of his eyes, and much of the rest of his

00:16:37.190 --> 00:16:38.360
right arm.

00:16:38.360 --> 00:16:43.449
His remaining eye was weeping, remembering
how his embrace, as the Old Man, had killed

00:16:43.449 --> 00:16:44.740
his beloved Anna.

00:16:44.740 --> 00:16:49.050
He’d lost his humanity and become the worst
kind of monster.

00:16:49.050 --> 00:16:52.649
The kind who even hurts the people he loves
most.

00:16:52.649 --> 00:16:57.230
SCP-035, floating in the darkness, was still
just laughing at him.

00:16:57.230 --> 00:17:00.490
“You’re pathetic, Scranton,” it said.

00:17:00.490 --> 00:17:05.060
“Look how little is left of you.

00:17:05.060 --> 00:17:07.000
You haven’t even been human in decades!

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:10.080
Why not give up what little is left?

00:17:10.080 --> 00:17:17.150
You’re mine now, and soon, you’re going
to be nothing at all.”

00:17:17.150 --> 00:17:22.040
And Dr. Scranton kept crying, because he feared
the Mask was right.

00:17:22.040 --> 00:17:26.560
Back in the city, the stolen police cruiser
pulled up in front of a preschool, and the

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:28.380
Masked Old Man got out.

00:17:28.380 --> 00:17:32.270
This would be the perfect place for his next
little slice of fun.

00:17:32.270 --> 00:17:36.220
Straightening himself up, he began walking
to the school, knowing that with the extent

00:17:36.220 --> 00:17:39.970
of his psychic powers, nobody would be strong
enough to run away.

00:17:39.970 --> 00:17:43.270
They’d all just have to sit there and suffer.

00:17:43.270 --> 00:17:45.430
Just like Dr. Robert Scranton.

00:17:45.430 --> 00:17:48.660
“Goodbye, Old Man,” The Mask said to him.

00:17:48.660 --> 00:17:51.480
“I’m tired of talking to you now.”

00:17:51.480 --> 00:17:55.010
Dr. Scranton was ready to give up and let
himself disappear.

00:17:55.010 --> 00:17:56.500
But then...

00:17:56.500 --> 00:17:57.950
Something occurred to him.

00:17:57.950 --> 00:18:00.300
Knowledge from his Foundation days.

00:18:00.300 --> 00:18:01.300
“I...

00:18:01.300 --> 00:18:04.250
I must be wearing you,” Dr. Scranton said.

00:18:04.250 --> 00:18:06.450
“I must be wearing you!”

00:18:06.450 --> 00:18:10.810
Scranton reached up to his face with his remaining
hand, grasping at something.

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:14.740
Suddenly, the face of the floating Mask twisted
into an infuriated frown,

00:18:14.740 --> 00:18:16.330
“What do you think you’re doing?”

00:18:16.330 --> 00:18:17.330
It said.

00:18:17.330 --> 00:18:18.780
“It’s too late, Robert.”

00:18:18.780 --> 00:18:21.200
But Scranton wouldn’t be deterred.

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:25.550
He gripped something invisible over his face
and began to tug, even though pulling on this

00:18:25.550 --> 00:18:28.550
invisible mask on his face was agonizing.

00:18:28.550 --> 00:18:35.290
The whole void around him began to shake and
quiver, including the grimacing SCP-035.

00:18:35.290 --> 00:18:37.180
Scranton just kept pulling.

00:18:37.180 --> 00:18:38.930
“Stop that, you idiot!”

00:18:38.930 --> 00:18:39.930
It roared.

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:42.140
“Stop it, stop it, stop it!

00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:45.200
You’re going to ruin everything, you—“

00:18:45.200 --> 00:18:46.920
But it was already too late.

00:18:46.920 --> 00:18:52.080
Dr. Scranton murmured, “I’m sorry, Anna”,
and gave one last yank.

00:18:52.080 --> 00:18:54.780
That’s when everything went white.

00:18:54.780 --> 00:18:58.880
Back in the city, it thankfully wasn’t long
until a group of Mobile Task Force agents

00:18:58.880 --> 00:19:01.390
was able to locate the two anomalies.

00:19:01.390 --> 00:19:07.480
SCP-106 was sitting cross-legged on the grass
outside a pre-school - where, thankfully,

00:19:07.480 --> 00:19:11.100
nobody had been hurt - and just staring off
into space.

00:19:11.100 --> 00:19:16.020
In his trembling hands was another familiar
sight: a frowning SCP-035.

00:19:16.020 --> 00:19:19.030
Now go check out “The Whole Story!

00:19:19.030 --> 00:19:22.960
- What if SCP-096 Wore SCP-035?”

00:19:22.960 --> 00:19:28.320
and “SCP-106 - The Old Man Origin Theories”
for more tales concerning today’s terrifying

00:19:28.320 --> 00:19:28.360
anomalies!

